    "index_entries": 8370,
    "index_meta_files": 1,
    "payload": "UnityFS asset bundles; each holds two Texture2D (1024x1024 card face + 512x512 auxiliary)",
    "entry_id_scheme": "<english-set-code>_en_<english-card-number>, e.g. files/sv1_en_001"
  },
  "method": {
    "extraction": "tools/asar-inspect/cli.mjs (read-only asar pickle+JSON index reader)",
    "decode": "tools/card-image-export/export_textures.py (UnityPy, PNG export)",
    "ocr": "tools/ocr/ocr-windows.ps1 (Windows OCR, zh-Hans-CN)",
    "screen": "tools/card-image-export/screen_evidence.mjs (bounded per-entry pipeline)",
    "bound": "exploratory passes only; the full pack was never walked entry-by-entry for decoding"
  },
  "findings": [
    "The `_en_` id suffix and the \"EN\" segment inside the MaterialManifest asset path are naming conventions, not evidence of the language printed on the card.",
    "Sampled card faces are predominantly Traditional Chinese (zh-Hant) for SWSH/SV-era sets, with occasional Simplified Chinese (zh-Hans) and English faces.",
    "Card faces carry a visible printed collector number (e.g. SV1F 001/078, 1/214, 78/101) and a regulation mark; these come from the image itself, not from the id.",
    "Ids follow English set codes and English card numbers; the printed number on a Chinese face can differ from that id (e.g. sv1_en_170 prints as SV1F 069/078).",
    "No right/product-owner statement ships with the pack; redistribution scope is unresolved and the pack must stay a local, user-configured input."
  ],
